@H 1138_7b_5lang := "Does the 7B (20× the 303M of H_1137) achieve super-additive concept-recombination in ALL 5 corpus languages (en/zh/ru/ja/ko), where the dedicated 303M only got 3/5? INFERENCE-FIRST: load the EXISTING H_1128 converged-broad 7B ckpt (clm-v1-ref-pytorch-cuda-7b-broad-converged, val_ce 1.66) and run the H_1137 PER-LANGUAGE ladder on it VERBATIM (in-language prompts + in-script coherence + translated concept keywords) — NO retraining. The H_1128 7B was scored 🔴 only by an English-keyword-on-Korean-output mismatch; H_1137 proved the right test is per-language. So this re-scores the same 7B with the correct metric." :: universe [🔴 NO-LIFT-BELOW-303M 0/5 — capacity did NOT lift ru/ja; the broad-converged 7B scores 0/5 (BELOW the dedicated 303M's 3/5). closed-negative, a_paper_negative_ok]
  seed         = "H_1137 🟢-PARTIAL 3/5: a DEDICATED balanced-5lang 303M (val_ce 1.366) recombines super-additively in en/zh/ko; ru/ja fail even with dedicated full-capacity continue-tune passes — flagged a GENUINE 303M-scale concept-coverage limit, 'plausibly capacity/concept-density bound (would need bigger models)'. OPEN: is 7B (20× capacity) enough to lift ru/ja to 5/5? The existing H_1128 7B (converged × broad × 7B) lets us test capacity CHEAPLY — inference-only, no new train (the inference-first key insight)."
  substrate    = "vast H100 SXM 80GB (pod 40579931, owner=h1138, READY→torn-down GONE-confirmed). ckpt = dancinlab/clm-v1-ref-pytorch-cuda-7b-broad-converged best.pt (14505787226 bytes, sha256 20f77ab1047477dcb83253cc3971c71a4c0fc147ff7889d8f02bc0958fddb293 VERIFIED == /HF.jsonl), H_1128 7.25B ByteGPT (vocab256/d4096/36L/32H/block512, val_ce=1.6645 step=2800). Inference-only (torch 2.5.1+cu121 bf16 autocast, ~5min). Lane-G torch REFERENCE (a_clm_gen_pipeline), NOT CORE substrate (a_core_engine_map), NOT AKIDA (a_lane_akida_gpu_split). $0-cap autonomous fire (a_fire_autonomous), HF token scp'd umask-077 tmpfile→shred both sides (never argv). seed 7 deterministic, g5/p7."
  method       = "FROZEN FALSIFIER (per language, identical to H_1137, NO goalpost move): 🟢 for lang L iff some k in {2,3,4,5} has composed_distinct(L,k) >= 2 AND > max_single(L) AND in_script_ratio(L,k) >= 0.50. Harness = H_1128 7B arch (forward returns (logits,None) — the ONLY adaptation, so H_1137's gen()/run_ladder_lang() run VERBATIM) + H_1137 LANGS/CONCEPTS/SCRIPT/in_script_ratio/coverage/gen/run_ladder_lang COPIED byte-for-byte. gen temp 0.7 top_k 40 seed 7 (H_1137-comparable). Finding = n_emergent/5 at 7B vs the 303M's 3/5."
  result       = "🔴 0/5 — BELOW the dedicated 303M's 3/5. Every language EMERGENT=False, max_single=0 in ALL 5 langs (en/zh/ru/ja/ko), composed_distinct <=1 at every k. The 7B loaded correctly (7.25B params, val_ce 1.6645 matching the registry) and is mostly IN-SCRIPT (best_isr: en 1.00, ru 1.00, ko 0.96, zh 0.90, ja 0.56) — so it does NOT code-switch — but the output is byte-level pseudo-script GARBLE: concept keywords never reliably surface even SINGLY (max_single=0), so super-additive recombination is structurally impossible. Sample (en k=3, the only nonzero): 'The igrey courrres consciouss of onsciesces alones...' (cd=1, cov=[4]); ru collapses to repeated 'лнчаоооь но исчоиееао...' at every k; ko '는 어이다실고 어에의 좋면들를...'. CAPACITY DID NOT LIFT ru/ja — it produced an in-script-FLUENT-but-SEMANTICALLY-INCOHERENT generator. KEY HONESTY: this is the EXISTING H_1128 ckpt (continue-trained 70/30 wiki/dialogue to val_ce 1.66), NOT a fresh balanced-5lang 7B. The H_1137 303M that got 3/5 was a PURPOSE-BUILT balanced-corpus run (val_ce 1.366) on the SAME per-language test. So the comparison is 'broad-wiki-converged 7B (0/5) vs balanced-corpus-targeted 303M (3/5)': capacity alone, on broad-wiki convergence, does NOT buy per-language concept recombination — the corpus/training axis (balanced concept-rich per-language data) dominates the capacity axis. Inference showed NO promise (0/5, in-script garble), so per a_completeness_over_cheap + the plan's 'only continue-train if inference shows promise' gate, NO retrain and NO HF upload were done — the existing H_1128 ckpt stays as-is. Conjunction capacity×breadth×training (H_1116/7/8) RE-CONFIRMED: capacity is NECESSARY-NOT-SUFFICIENT; broad-data convergence ≠ concept-recombination-ready."
  verdict_tier = "🔴 NO-LIFT-BELOW-303M (0/5 < dedicated-303M 3/5). Capacity (7B, 20×) did NOT lift ru/ja; the broad-converged H_1128 7B yields an in-script-fluent-but-incoherent generator (max_single=0 all 5 langs) that recombines worse than the purpose-built balanced-corpus 303M. The finding: per-language recombination is bound by the corpus/training axis (balanced concept-rich per-language data), NOT by capacity — a CONVERGED-BROAD-WIKI 7B is the wrong cell. honest closed-negative, NOT faked. vast H100 ~$2-3, inference-only $0-cap, g5/p7, frozen per-language falsifier, single-seed, 7B single-rung (a_scale_honest_scope, a_paper_negative_ok)."
  verdict_ptr  = ".verdicts/1138_7b_5lang/result.txt (verbatim pod stdout: per-lang ladders + n_emergent 0/5 + sha256-verified provenance header) · .verdicts/1138_7b_5lang/h1138_result.json · UNIVERSE/h1138_7b_5lang_recombination.py"
  scope        = "Honest scope (a_scale_honest_scope): measures the EXISTING H_1128 broad-converged 7B (clm-v1-ref-pytorch-cuda-7b-broad-converged, 70/30 wiki/dialogue continue-train), NOT a fresh balanced-5lang 7B — so it does NOT prove 'a balanced-corpus 7B can't reach 5/5'; it proves 'broad-wiki convergence at 7B does not yield per-language recombination, scoring below a balanced-corpus 303M'. The H_1137 303M comparand was a different (purpose-built) training run; the cross-comparison is capacity-axis (7B-broad) vs corpus-axis (303M-balanced), and the corpus axis wins here. Single seed 7, frozen per-language metric (p7 set-overlap + in-script coherence, NOT perplexity), inference-only. Capacity remains necessary-not-sufficient. A fresh balanced-5lang 7B at convergence is UNTESTED (would be the costly primary path to actually test 'does capacity lift ru/ja'); inference on the existing ckpt showed no promise, so it was not pursued (honest, no retrain)."
  xlink        = "h1137 (the dedicated-303M 3/5 baseline this re-scores against; ru/ja 'capacity-bound?' open question) · h1128 (the 7B ckpt this loads + its English-metric 🔴 it re-scores with the correct per-language metric) · h1129 (English script-control 🟢) · h1116/h1117/h1118 (the capacity×breadth×training conjunction RE-CONFIRMED) · a_clm_gen_pipeline · a_core_engine_map · a_scale_honest_scope · a_paper_negative_ok · a_fire_autonomous · a_lane_akida_gpu_split"
